                <pb facs="0428" n="383" xml:id="pg383"/>

                <head>140. Memorandum From Secretary of State Vance to President Carter<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d140-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-04-25">April 25, 1979</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to India]</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Vajpayee</hi>. We devoted today’s meeting with Vajpayee
                    to a variety of multilateral issues and the nuclear question.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d140-f2"/> I urged the Indians to support UNEF renewal,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d140-f3"/> and to resist attempts to expel Egypt and Israel from UN
                    organizations. Vajpayee was non-committal on the first issue but stated that
                    India would oppose expulsion efforts in UN organizations or in the NAM. In the
                    nuclear discussion, he indicated a willingness to explore regional solutions if
                    China could be included in some way. We urged him to reconsider his opposition
                    to a joint Indo-Pakistani statement on the non-development of nuclear
                    weapons.</p>
                <p>I think our talks have succeeded in demonstrating our deep concern on the nuclear
                    issue while underlining the broad areas of agreement in our bilateral relations.
                    Vajpayee seems to accept the concept that we have a <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >mutual</hi> problem in Pakistan.</p>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to India]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d140-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d140-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Subject
                    File, Box 21, Evening Reports (State): 4/79. Secret. Carter initialed at the top
                    of the memorandum.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d140-f2" n="2" xml:id="d140-f2-content">
                <p>The April 25 meeting was the second of two discussions between Vance and
                    Vajpayee. The first took place on April 24; see <ref target="#d138">Document
                        138</ref>. No memorandum of conversation of the April 25 meeting was
                    found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d140-f3" n="3" xml:id="d140-f3-content">
                <p>The UNEF II was deployed in the Sinai Peninsula from October 1973 to July 1979
                    for the purpose of supervising the cease-fire after the October 1973
                    Arab-Israeli war and facilitating the redeployment of Egyptian and Israeli
                    forces in the area.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
